      "title": "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Given that $y = 7\\ln x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\ln x) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\ln x) \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
